      "math_academy_id": "e-5054",
      "problem": "Plot the graph of $y=-(x+1)^3-3.$",
      "worked_solution": "The given function can be obtained by translating $y=-x^3$ both horizontally and vertically.\n\nWe have two translations:\n\n- the $\\color{red}+1$ inside the parentheses means a horizontal translation of $1$ unit to the *left*, and\n\n- the $\\color{blue}-3$ outside the parentheses means a vertical translation of $3$ units *down*.\n\nSo, the new graph looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14216079/assets/b5f3fac4f76321abdd825c6e7d5ab5b60916149bbffc7a94a8bd3e932c17d8ea.png)",
